n Lane"},"message":"Kin Score 0.12.0 rescore artifacts (2026-08-19)","tree":{"sha":"de96c284715f54bf5720d509e1549a19a8bc3e23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/api-evangelist/commerce-layer/git/trees/de96c284715f54bf5720d509e1549a19a8bc3e23"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/api-evangelist/commerce-layer/git/commits/33d3c16ab5f94e779aee93191d1c16f45a013613","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56100?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kinlane","id":56100,"login":"kinlane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTAw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/api-evangelist/commerce-layer/commit/33d3c16ab5f94e779aee93191d1c16f45a013613","node_id":"C_kwDOSnCHyNoAKDMzZDNjMTZhYjVmOTRlNzc5YWVlOTMxOTFkMWMxNmY0NWEwMTM2MTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/api-evangelist/commerce-layer/commit/10f608aebcc7ad0da474a9d9c952fb1a93b51531","sha":"10f608aebcc7ad0da474a9d9c952fb1a93b51531","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/api-evangelist/commerce-layer/commits/10f608aebcc7ad0da474a9d9c952fb1a93b51531"}],"sha":"33d3c16ab5f94e779aee93191d1c16f45a013613","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/api-evangelist/commerce-layer/commits/33d3c16ab5f94e779aee93191d1c16f45a013613"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56100?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kinlane","id":56100,"login":"kinlane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTAw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/api-evangelist/commerce-layer/commits/10f608aebcc7ad0da474a9d9c952fb1a93b51531/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T13:58:49Z","email":"kinlane@gmail.com","name":"Kin Lane"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T13:58:49Z","email":"kinlane@gmail.com","name":"Kin Lane"},"message":"Kin Score 0.12.0 — rescore, pointer probe, authorship provenance\n\nRubric 0.12.0 replaces 0.11.0 across the catalog. Nineteen roadmap items shipped\ntogether because several move the same providers, and batching them means one band\nrecalibration instead of three.\n\nWHAT CHANGED IN THIS REPO\n\n  kin/score-<ts>.yml    rescored at rubric 0.12.0\n  llms/                 llms.txt harvested and verified, or a negative probe record\n  rules/                authorship stamped where the file names its own generator\n  apis.yml              pointer type spellings normalised toward APIs.json 0.22\n\nTHE RELEASE\n\nPointer liveness (roadmap#16) is 84% of the movement. All 117,876 distinct scored\npointer URLs were fetched against a per-host control: 73,343 instances (5.5%) are\nconfirmed dead and had been credited as if they resolved. Checks now grade live\n1.00 / unverified 0.50 / dead 0.00. Composite mean -1.30; 13,056 providers down,\nzero up from this change alone.\n\n5,214 pointers are OUR limit, not the provider''s — refused to a declared crawler,\nbehind a JS challenge, or unreachable. Those grade live or unverified, never dead.\nWithout that split 1,885 providers would have been marked down for an ordinary\nedge policy.\n\nFacets renamed: governance -> contract_governance (it scores artifacts describing\na CONTRACT, never how an organisation governs itself) and commercial_clarity ->\naccess_clarity (for a free statutory interface the word commercial describes\nnothing). Both keys are emitted side by side for 0.12.x; the old ones drop at 1.0.\n\nRegulatory scoring is now regime-relative: composite = base + w*(reg - regime_mean).\nBeing correctly identified as regulated had been a PENALTY of -1.06 on average while\nthin tagging was a reward. Composite is clamped to [0,100] because re-centring\nsubtracts a constant and could otherwise go negative.\n\nApplicability: dry_run_mode and idempotency are `na` for the 1,008 providers whose\nsurface is entirely read-only — a GET is idempotent by definition, and every request\nto a read API already is a dry run. 24 of access_clarity''s 38 points are `na` for the\n212 providers with no commercial surface by design.\n\nNew: lifecycle_documented, domain_standard_conformance, reversibility_documented.\nProtobuf/gRPC and WSDL now count as contracts — 45 providers were recorded as\npublishing nothing while holding 5,526 RPCs or 1,363 SOAP operations.\n\nmcp_server reads deployment truth instead of a pointer; 2,503 derived candidates\nlose credit they never earned. contract_governance dropped zero_errors and\nlow_error_density — both read declared severities while promising lint outcomes, and\ntogether made the scoring-optimal ruleset one that could never fail a build.\n\nRecorded but not scored: operator (who produced each artifact), interface_styles\n(442 rpc-http vs 5,551 rest), needs_work (3,659 records, every one owner=catalog),\ndisclosure_states, and the accountability layer schema.\n\nBands re-cut to hold the documented distribution; every band within 0.1pp. Agent\nreadiness bands unchanged.\n\nFull detail: api-evangelist/kin-score CHANGELOG.md and ROADMAP.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2a2999a06eedfb2d897be76be9e45f6c1e658658","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/api-evangelist/commerce-layer/git/trees/2a2999a06eedfb2d897be76be9e45f6c1e658658"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/api-evangelist/commerce-layer/git/commits/10f608aebcc7ad0da474a9d9c952fb1a93b51531","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56100?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kinlane","id":56100,"login":"kinlane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTAw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/api-evangelist/commerce-layer/commit/10f608aebcc7ad0da474a9d9c952fb1a93b51531","node_id":"C_kwDOSnCHyN