er","id":74619832,"login":"jajjer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NjE5ODMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/10e74d1816b9cffc91cb467e3a38895c2b31e27c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T18:06:44Z","email":"jaj.jacob.jensen@gmail.com","name":"Jacob Jensen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T18:06:44Z","email":"jaj.jacob.jensen@gmail.com","name":"Jacob Jensen"},"message":"Remove stale ''scaffolding only'' status banner from README\n\nThe note dated to commit 1 of the spike, when the algorithm and\nendpoint hadn''t been written yet. Both are now implemented, deployed,\nand covered by 101 tests across the backend, frontend, and E2E layers.\nLeaving the banner in place would be misleading to anyone landing on\nthe repo from the Talk thread.","tree":{"sha":"fa07a057dab681f49fc9f1c24eb21cc08b58b4fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/git/trees/fa07a057dab681f49fc9f1c24eb21cc08b58b4fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/git/commits/10e74d1816b9cffc91cb467e3a38895c2b31e27c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74619832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer","id":74619832,"login":"jajjer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NjE5ODMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commit/10e74d1816b9cffc91cb467e3a38895c2b31e27c","node_id":"C_kwDOSn6E69oAKDEwZTc0ZDE4MTZiOWNmZmM5MWNiNDY3ZTNhMzg4OTVjMmIzMWUyN2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commit/b813736b09bbfb66be4fe5732136f8fc7329b3a1","sha":"b813736b09bbfb66be4fe5732136f8fc7329b3a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/b813736b09bbfb66be4fe5732136f8fc7329b3a1"}],"sha":"10e74d1816b9cffc91cb467e3a38895c2b31e27c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/10e74d1816b9cffc91cb467e3a38895c2b31e27c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74619832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer","id":74619832,"login":"jajjer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NjE5ODMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/b813736b09bbfb66be4fe5732136f8fc7329b3a1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T16:45:44Z","email":"jaj.jacob.jensen@gmail.com","name":"Jacob Jensen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T16:45:44Z","email":"jaj.jacob.jensen@gmail.com","name":"Jacob Jensen"},"message":"Production-readiness round: audit, fail-open, bounded LRU\n\nThree production-blocking gaps closed. All backend tests (now 80) pass;\nintegration verification confirmed for two of three.\n\n1. Structured audit logging (cdshooks.audit logger)\n   New CdsAuditLogger emits a JSON line per CDS-Hooks invocation:\n   timestamp, hookInstance, userId, patientUuid, drugs[], matches[],\n   outcome (SUCCESS / NO_DATA / UNAVAILABLE). Ops teams route the\n   dedicated ''cdshooks.audit'' SLF4J logger separately (syslog, Splunk,\n   etc.) for HIPAA / governance review. CdsHooksServiceImpl now writes\n   one audit record per invocation regardless of outcome. 5 tests pin\n   the record schema.\n\n2. Fail-open with explicit ''allergy check unavailable'' Card\n   When the matching algorithm cannot run, the service now returns a\n   Card with indicator=info and the message ''Allergy check unavailable\n   — verify recorded allergies in the patient chart before proceeding\n   with this order''. Silent empty response would be interpreted as ''no\n   warnings'' and could mask a real conflict — wrong patient-safety\n   default.\n\n   SnowstormClient.fhirGet now distinguishes:\n     - 2xx: parsed body\n     - 4xx: null (legitimate ''no data'' from terminology server)\n     - 5xx / IOException / interrupt: throws TerminologyUnavailableException\n\n   The service catches anything that propagates out of the matcher and\n   converts it to an unavailable card. Unit test\n   (matcherThrows_returnsUnavailableCard) verifies the path.\n\n   Known integration gap (task #28): changing cdshooks.snowstormUrl via\n   REST is not picked up by SnowstormClient under some auth contexts —\n   gp() silently returns null and baseUrl() falls back to default.\n   Separate small bug from the fail-open feature itself.\n\n3. Bounded LRU cache (replaces unbounded TtlCache)\n   TtlCache is now backed by access-order LinkedHashMap with an LRU\n   eviction policy; max entries configurable via the new\n   cdshooks.cacheMaxEntries GP (default 10_000). Without this, sustained\n   traffic that touches a wide working set of concepts would grow the\n   in-memory cache without limit and eventually OOM the JVM. 3 new\n   tests cover the eviction bound, LRU recency, and invalid bounds.\n\nTest totals after this round:\n  Backend Java: 80 (was 61)\n  Frontend:     19\n  E2E:           2\n  Total:       101","tree":{"sha":"ac5b5fb76a173609b46f3629fbda24d2c8d7d6bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/git/trees/ac5b5fb76a173609b46f3629fbda24d2c8d7d6bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/git/commits/b813736b09bbfb66be4fe5732136f8fc7329b3a1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74619832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer","id":74619832,"login":"jajjer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NjE5ODMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commit/b813736b09bbfb66be4fe5732136f8fc7329b3a1","node_id":"C_kwDOSn6E69oAKGI4MTM3MzZiMDliYmZiNjZiZTRmZTU3MzIxMzZmOGZjNzMyOWIzYTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commit/35ff563bd6e4c3fd757e04c1c047a43d9eb2f847","sha":"35ff563bd6e4c3fd757e04c1c047a43d9eb2f847","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/35ff563bd6e4c3fd757e04c1c047a43d9eb2f847"}],"sha":"b813736b09bbfb66be4fe5732136f8fc7329b3a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/b813736b09bbfb66be4fe5732136f8fc7329b3a1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74619832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer","id":74619832,"login":"jajjer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NjE5ODMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/35ff563bd6e4c3fd757e04c1c047a43d9eb2f847/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T05:14:50Z","email":"jaj.jacob.jensen@gmail.com","name":"Jacob Jensen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T05:14:50Z","email":"jaj.jacob.jensen@gmail.com","name":"Jacob Jensen"},"message":"Comprehensive test coverage round + patient-safety fix\n\nAdded 67 tests across all the gaps. Total test count now:\n  Java backend: 61 (was 11)\n  Frontend:     19 (was 5)\n  E2E:          2  (unchanged; click-through still .skip)\n\nPatient-safety fix\n------------------\nSeverityMapper used String.contains(\"severe\"), which would have\nclassified CIEL concepts like ''Severe sepsis'' (112480), ''Severe anaemia''\n(162044), and ''Severe malaria'' (160155) as severity=SEVERE. That would\nescalate their associated CDS Cards from warning to critical (the\nindicator mapping is SEVERE -> critical), altering clinical priority.\nReplaced with exact case-insensitive equality and covered with explicit\n''this clinical finding should NOT map to SEVERE'' tests.\n\nNew test classes\n----------------\nJava:\n  SeverityMapperTest              13 tests (severity mapping + indicator + bug regression)\n  SnomedMappingExtractorTest      10 tests (SNOMED source detection, edge cases)\n  TtlCacheTest                     5 tests (TTL eviction, multi-key, invalidate, null values)\n  SubsumptionOutcomeTest           4 tests (FHIR code parsing, indicatesAncestry semantics)\n  SnowstormClientParseTest        10 tests (FHIR Parameters parsing — refactored loadAttributeValues/loadSubsumes to expose pure parse helpers)\n  AllergyMatcherEdgeCasesTest     10 tests (multi-allergy, multi-ingredient, equivalent outcome, direct substance mapping, dedup, null inputs)\n  ForwardingFilterTest             8 tests (JWT validate, bad sig, expired, issuer mismatch, malformed, tampered claims, no subject — refactored verifyAndExtractSubject to take expectedIssuer as a parameter so it''s testable without OpenMRS Context)\n\nFrontend:\n  medication.resource.test.ts      7 tests (extractDrugSnomed pure helper)\n  cds-hooks.resource.test.ts       3 tests (buildCdsHooksRequestBody)\n  drug-allergy-alert.extension.test.tsx +4 tests (multi-card render, indicator->kind mapping for warning/info/critical)\n\nInfrastructure\n--------------\n- Pinned jackson-core and jackson-annotations explicitly in the parent\n  POM. Without this the test classpath inherited an older jackson-core\n  from OpenMRS transitives that didn''t match jackson-databind 2.15.4,\n  producing NoClassDefFoundError on StreamConstraintsException.\n- Extracted SnowstormClient parse* methods to package-private statics\n  so the JSON interpretation is testable without an HTTP server.\n- Made ForwardingFilter.verifyAndExtractSubject take expectedIssuer\n  explicitly (instead of reading it from Context inside) so the JWT\n  verification path is testable without OpenMRS.\n- Exported extractDrugSnomed and buildCdsHooksRequestBody from their\n  respective frontend resource modules.","tree":{"sha":"fba1b8672274f7444112bb7528e69afd67d5d03e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/git/trees/fba1b8672274f7444112bb7528e69afd67d5d03e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/git/commits/35ff563bd6e4c3fd757e04c1c047a43d9eb2f847","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74619832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer","id":74619832,"login":"jajjer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NjE5ODMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commit/35ff563bd6e4c3fd757e04c1c047a43d9eb2f847","node_id":"C_kwDOSn6E69oAKDM1ZmY1NjNiZDZlNGMzZmQ3NTdlMDRjMWMwNDdhNDNkOWViMmY4NDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commit/e82af9c4cc29e51f850dbe1ad2e50765fa83cd08","sha":"e82af9c4cc29e51f850dbe1ad2e50765fa83cd08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/e82af9c4cc29e51f850dbe1ad2e50765fa83cd08"}],"sha":"35ff563bd6e4c3fd757e04c1c047a43d9eb2f847","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/35ff563bd6e4c3fd757e04c1c047a43d9eb2f847"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74619832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer","id":74619832,"login":"jajjer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NjE5ODMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/e82af9c4cc29e51f850dbe1ad2e50765fa83cd08/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T05:01:06Z","email":"jaj.jacob.jensen@gmail.com","name":"Jacob Jensen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T05:01:06Z","email":"jaj.jacob.jensen@gmail.com","name":"Jacob Jensen"},"message":"Bearer-token auth + frontend wiring + RTL + E2E tests\n\nFour follow-ups completed in this round.\n\n1) JWT bearer-token auth (HS256). The ForwardingFilter now also handles\n   Authorization: Bearer headers: validates the JWT with the HMAC secret\n   configured in cdshooks.bearerHmacSecret, opens an OpenMRS session as\n   the user named in the sub claim, and forwards. Falls through to the\n   existing OpenMRS auth filters (session cookie, basic) when no bearer\n   header is present. Verified live: bad bearer token + no secret -> 401;\n   basic auth + no bearer -> 200; filter log line confirms the path.\n\n   The standalone BearerTokenAuthFilter class was deleted because the\n   module-filter URL pattern matching for /ws/cds-services/* wasn''t\n   firing reliably; consolidating both concerns into the ForwardingFilter\n   (which DOES fire — we have a stack trace for it) is more robust.\n\n   The previous proxy-privilege workaround in CdsHooksServiceImpl is\n   retained because basic-auth and anonymous flows still need it; it''s a\n   no-op once bearer auth establishes a real user context.\n\n2) Frontend wired into the running SPA. Bundle copied into the frontend\n   container at /usr/share/nginx/html/openmrs-esm-cdshooks-app-1.0.0/,\n   importmap.json patched to include @openmrs/esm-cdshooks-app, and\n   routes.registry.json patched to declare the drug-allergy-alert\n   extension on order-item-additional-info-slot. Bundle verified\n   reachable through the gateway with HTTP 200.\n\n3) React Testing Library coverage. Five tests pass: no SNOMED code ->\n   silent; backend empty -> silent; critical card -> renders Carbon\n   InlineNotification with role=status containing the summary, detail,\n   and recorded reaction; backend error -> visible ''unavailable'' notice;\n   loading -> silent.\n\n4) Playwright E2E. Two runnable specs pass: a direct backend smoke\n   asserting the critical Card is returned end-to-end for our test\n   patient + Amoxicillin SNOMED code, and a SPA-level check that the\n   cdshooks module is registered in /spa/importmap.json at runtime. A\n   third spec — clicking through the medication-order workspace to\n   verify the InlineNotification renders inline — is intentionally\n   .skip pending stable selectors (data-testid attributes) on the\n   host esm-patient-medications-app.","tree":{"sha":"064293041cf2a9a688e6930ec4efde680d31faec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/git/trees/064293041cf2a9a688e6930ec4efde680d31faec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/git/commits/e82af9c4cc29e51f850dbe1ad2e50765fa83cd08","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74619832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer","id":74619832,"login":"jajjer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NjE5ODMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commit/e82af9c4cc29e51f850dbe1ad2e50765fa83cd08","node_id":"C_kwDOSn6E69oAKGU4MmFmOWM0Y2MyOWU1MWY4NTBkYmUxYWQyZTUwNzY1ZmE4M2NkMDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commit/89dc4172f2c364aa96dbd314e11b3f70b233fa26","sha":"89dc4172f2c364aa96dbd314e11b3f70b233fa26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/89dc4172f2c364aa96dbd314e11b3f70b233fa26"}],"sha":"e82af9c4cc29e51f850dbe1ad2e50765fa83cd08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/e82af9c4cc29e51f850dbe1ad2e50765fa83cd08"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74619832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer","id":74619832,"login":"jajjer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NjE5ODMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/89dc4172f2c364aa96dbd314e11b3f70b233fa26/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T04:43:31Z","email":"jaj.jacob.jensen@gmail.com","name":"Jacob Jensen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T04:43:31Z","email":"jaj.jacob.jensen@gmail.com","name":"Jacob Jensen"},"message":"Scaffold the esm-cdshooks-app frontend microfrontend\n\nAdds a new SPA package at frontend/esm-cdshooks-app/ that registers a\nsingle extension into order-item-additional-info-slot — the slot\nesm-patient-medications-app exposes on each line of the medication\norder basket. The extension:\n\n  1. Picks up the drug UUID from extension state + the patient UUID from\n     the patient-chart context.\n  2. Resolves the drug to its SNOMED CT code via the FHIR2 module''s\n     Medication resource (which already emits mapped reference terms\n     via ConceptTranslator).\n  3. POSTs a CDS-Hooks 2.0 medication-prescribe request to the backend\n     module at /openmrs/ws/cds-services/drug-allergy.\n  4. Renders each returned Card as a Carbon InlineNotification tiered\n     by severity (critical -> error, warning -> warning, info -> info).\n  5. On backend error, surfaces a visible ''allergy check unavailable''\n     notification rather than failing silently — patient safety beats\n     UI cleanliness.\n\nBuilt artifact confirmed: webpack produces a SystemJS bundle at\ndist/openmrs-esm-cdshooks-app.js (~4 KiB) with all OpenMRS framework\nimports correctly externalized for the SPA import map.\n\nPre-shipping work:\n  - npm install ships its own dependency conflicts (React 19 vs 18 peer\n    deps); --legacy-peer-deps works for now.\n  - tsc --noEmit complains about the framework''s .ts sources (missing\n    rxjs types, etc.); ignore those — the webpack build doesn''t see them.\n  - Need unit tests with React Testing Library.\n  - Need to be added to the RefApp''s spa-assemble-config.json before it\n    will load in a running SPA.","tree":{"sha":"b78efa04f581afa1159a49d0c4c6000404088c73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/git/trees/b78efa04f581afa1159a49d0c4c6000404088c73"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/git/commits/89dc4172f2c364aa96dbd314e11b3f70b233fa26","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74619832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer","id":74619832,"login":"jajjer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NjE5ODMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commit/89dc4172f2c364aa96dbd314e11b3f70b233fa26","node_id":"C_kwDOSn6E69oAKDg5ZGM0MTcyZjJjMzY0YWE5NmRiZDMxNGUxMWIzZjcwYjIzM2ZhMjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commit/51b7e094efadc15fc2c12c004a367f4f17b8467d","sha":"51b7e094efadc15fc2c12c004a367f4f17b8467d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/51b7e094efadc15fc2c12c004a367f4f17b8467d"}],"sha":"89dc4172f2c364aa96dbd314e11b3f70b233fa26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/89dc4172f2c364aa96dbd314e11b3f70b233fa26"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74619832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer","id":74619832,"login":"jajjer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NjE5ODMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/51b7e094efadc15fc2c12c004a367f4f17b8467d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T04:37:56Z","email":"jaj.jacob.jensen@gmail.com","name":"Jacob Jensen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T04:37:56Z","email":"jaj.jacob.jensen@gmail.com","name":"Jacob Jensen"},"message":"Filter noisy class matches; allow basic-auth + anonymous CDS-Hooks calls\n\nTwo follow-ups from the end-to-end demo, both verified live against the\nisolated cdshooks-dev stack:\n\n1. AllergyMatcherImpl.expandToSubstances() previously included the seed\n   SCTID unconditionally, which produced trivially-true ''class'' matches\n   like ''Amoxicillin contains 27658006, which is a Pharmaceutical /\n   biologic product''. Now the seed is only used as a fallback when the\n   concept has no bridging attribute (Causative agent on findings or\n   Has active ingredient on products). With this change a real patient\n   with a penicillin allergy ordered Amoxicillin returns one clean\n   card instead of two:\n     ⚠ Allergy to penicillin (class match) [critical]\n       Amoxicillin contains Amoxicillin (substance), which is a\n       Penicillin — the causative-agent class for Allergy to penicillin.\n\n2. CdsHooksServiceImpl now adds Context proxy privileges (GET_PATIENTS,\n   GET_ALLERGIES, GET_CONCEPTS) around the PatientService calls. POST\n   now works with plain basic auth as well as session-cookie auth —\n   previously a non-cookie request would 500 with ''Privileges required:\n   Get Patients''. The privilege management is wrapped in a try/catch so\n   it fails soft in unit-test contexts where no UserContext exists.\n\nThis is a spike shortcut and is documented as such in code — the\nproduction path is bearer-token authentication per the CDS-Hooks 2.0\nsecurity spec.","tree":{"sha":"902113ec2911bc91b1eafa94d9457b1543daf835","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/git/trees/902113ec2911bc91b1eafa94d9457b1543daf835"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/git/commits/51b7e094efadc15fc2c12c004a367f4f17b8467d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74619832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer","id":74619832,"login":"jajjer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NjE5ODMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commit/51b7e094efadc15fc2c12c004a367f4f17b8467d","node_id":"C_kwDOSn6E69oAKDUxYjdlMDk0ZWZhZGMxNWZjMmMxMmMwMDRhMzY3ZjRmMTdiODQ2N2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commit/37967fc09dc27100fb088134feefa7c6534f4b51","sha":"37967fc09dc27100fb088134feefa7c6534f4b51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/37967fc09dc27100fb088134feefa7c6534f4b51"}],"sha":"51b7e094efadc15fc2c12c004a367f4f17b8467d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/51b7e094efadc15fc2c12c004a367f4f17b8467d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74619832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer","id":74619832,"login":"jajjer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NjE5ODMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/37967fc09dc27100fb088134feefa7c6534f4b51/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T04:23:08Z","email":"jaj.jacob.jensen@gmail.com","name":"Jacob Jensen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T04:23:08Z","email":"jaj.jacob.jensen@gmail.com","name":"Jacob Jensen"},"message":"End-to-end verified against a real patient\n\nDemoed the full pipeline against an isolated cdshooks-dev stack with a\ntest patient (Alice Penicillin-Test) carrying a recorded coded allergy\nto penicillin (severity Severe, reaction Hepatotoxicity). POSTing a\nmedication-prescribe hook with an Amoxicillin SNOMED code (27658006)\nreturns a CDS-Hooks Card with indicator=critical and the explanation\n''Amoxicillin contains Amoxicillin (substance), which is a Penicillin''.\n\nRefactors and additions in this commit:\n\n- CdsHooksServiceImpl now uses a locale-independent concept-name\n  accessor (prefers English, falls back to any available name). The\n  previous Concept.getDisplayString() call reached into the OpenMRS\n  service context for locale resolution, which made unit-testing\n  impractical. The same refactor applies to SeverityMapper.\n\n- Added CdsHooksServiceImplTest with three mocked end-to-end cases\n  (unknown patient, patient with no allergies, severe-allergy class\n  match producing a critical Card). 11 tests now pass overall.\n\n- docs/DESIGN.md gained a ''Current Implementation Status'' section\n  with the live demo curl + sample Card response, plus a list of what\n  the spike validated and what remains.\n\n- docs/TALK_POST_DRAFT.md is a ready-to-paste reply for the OpenMRS\n  Talk thread, including direct questions for Andrew and Veronica and\n  a link back to this repo.","tree":{"sha":"74e61bc1ba430516001d6c6d49feb79deeb28592","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/git/trees/74e61bc1ba430516001d6c6d49feb79deeb28592"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/git/commits/37967fc09dc27100fb088134feefa7c6534f4b51","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74619832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer","id":74619832,"login":"jajjer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NjE5ODMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commit/37967fc09dc27100fb088134feefa7c6534f4b51","node_id":"C_kwDOSn6E69oAKDM3OTY3ZmMwOWRjMjcxMDBmYjA4ODEzNGZlZWZhN2M2NTM0ZjRiNTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commit/e5f59819a272badb743af3608fcde0d8dd256721","sha":"e5f59819a272badb743af3608fcde0d8dd256721","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/e5f59819a272badb743af3608fcde0d8dd256721"}],"sha":"37967fc09dc27100fb088134feefa7c6534f4b51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/37967fc09dc27100fb088134feefa7c6534f4b51"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74619832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer","id":74619832,"login":"jajjer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NjE5ODMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/e5f59819a272badb743af3608fcde0d8dd256721/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T04:13:45Z","email":"jaj.jacob.jensen@gmail.com","name":"Jacob Jensen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T04:13:45Z","email":"jaj.jacob.jensen@gmail.com","name":"Jacob Jensen"},"message":"Add ForwardingFilter for spec-compliant /ws/cds-services URL\n\nThe discovery and invocation endpoints now live at the CDS-Hooks 2.0\nspec-compliant /openmrs/ws/cds-services[/{serviceId}] URLs. The\nunderlying servlet stays at /ms/cdsServicesServlet — the new\nForwardingFilter rewrites incoming /ws/cds-services requests internally.\n\nTwo effects:\n- POST works without further CSRF configuration. The OpenMRS-wide\n  csrfguard.unprotected.WS rule (%servletContext%/ws/*) already exempts\n  the /ws/ prefix, so we inherit it for free.\n- URL matches the HL7 CDS-Hooks specification, so external EHR clients\n  hit /openmrs/ws/cds-services without needing to know about the\n  internal /ms/ servlet name.\n\nVerified end-to-end against the isolated cdshooks-dev stack:\n  GET  /openmrs/ws/cds-services            -> 200 + valid discovery JSON\n  POST /openmrs/ws/cds-services/drug-allergy (with session cookie)\n                                            -> 200 + {\"cards\":[],\"systemActions\":[]}","tree":{"sha":"f1625d617402f517d599b4bcf3fe79cd766ab79d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/git/trees/f1625d617402f517d599b4bcf3fe79cd766ab79d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/git/commits/e5f59819a272badb743af3608fcde0d8dd256721","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74619832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer","id":74619832,"login":"jajjer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NjE5ODMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commit/e5f59819a272badb743af3608fcde0d8dd256721","node_id":"C_kwDOSn6E69oAKGU1ZjU5ODE5YTI3MmJhZGI3NDNhZjM2MDhmY2RlMGQ4ZGQyNTY3MjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commit/fa87d49bbf477749d3988b70dd41690d441a27e7","sha":"fa87d49bbf477749d3988b70dd41690d441a27e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/fa87d49bbf477749d3988b70dd41690d441a27e7"}],"sha":"e5f59819a272badb743af3608fcde0d8dd256721","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/e5f59819a272badb743af3608fcde0d8dd256721"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74619832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer","id":74619832,"login":"jajjer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NjE5ODMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/commits/fa87d49bbf477749d3988b70dd41690d441a27e7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T03:47:22Z","email":"jaj.jacob.jensen@gmail.com","name":"Jacob Jensen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T03:47:22Z","email":"jaj.jacob.jensen@gmail.com","name":"Jacob Jensen"},"message":"Initial spike: OpenMRS CDS Hooks module with drug-allergy alert\n\nValidates a CDS-Hooks-based architecture for the OpenMRS Talk thread\n\"1:1 Allergy/Rx should trigger warning\".\n\nEnd-to-end working against OpenMRS 2.8.4:\n- Module loads cleanly\n- Servlet registers at /openmrs/ms/cdsServicesServlet\n- Discovery endpoint returns valid CDS-Hooks 2.0 JSON\n- 8 unit tests pass\n\nIncludes algorithm port from Python spike that bridges SNOMED''s parallel\nhierarchies (finding -> substance via Causative agent; product -> substance\nvia Has active ingredient) for drug-class allergy matching.\n\nSee docs/DESIGN.md for the full design proposal and docs/SPIKE_JOURNAL.md\nfor what was learned along the way.","tree":{"sha":"8cc988d5abe774bf3e29b5222eea8da97ed1ed94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/git/trees/8cc988d5abe774bf3e29b5222eea8da97ed1ed94"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jajjer/openmrs-module-cdshooks/git/commits/fa87d49bbf477749d3988b70dd41690d441a27e7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74619832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jajjer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jajjer","id":7461983